# Publishing Code — PlasticOS

## `make pr` is the only publication command

```bash
make pr
```

`make pr` checks the feature branch, runs L4, runs the local gates, pushes once, and opens or reuses the pull request into `Staging`. `make pr base=<branch>` stacks onto an open parent pull request whose base is `Staging`. Merge is a separate human decision.

Use **`make commit`** separately to stage and commit. The commit target does not launch `make pr`.

**Never publish with raw `git push`, `make push`, or the GitHub API.** `make push` exits 1. `scripts/api_push.py` refuses API publication. Do not disable TLS verification to push.

---

## API publication is refused

A git transport failure is not a reason to publish through the API. Fix the transport, then run `make pr` again. `make api-push-check` only confirms that the API path stays refused.

---

## Permanent Fix

Keep the git object store **outside** cloud-sync folders (Dropbox, iCloud). Clone to a local dev path (e.g. `~/dev/IB-Odoo_19`). GitHub is the source of truth — never rely on Dropbox sync of `.git/`.

**Authority:** Global `97-governance-ssot-paths.mdc` — no `/Users/<user>/` paths in rules or scripts.

---

## Branch Model

- **`Staging`** = dev branch — all PRs target this
- **`Production`** = prod/main — promote from Staging when CI is green
- Never push feature branches directly to `Production`

### Branch names are capitalized — `Staging` / `Production` (not `staging`/`production`)

The canonical remote/local branches are **`Staging`** and **`Production`** with a capital first letter. macOS has a case-insensitive filesystem, so `git checkout staging` silently resolves to the local `Staging` branch and git prints `Switched to branch 'staging'` — this is the *same* ref, not a new one. Always use the capitalized form (`git checkout Staging`, `make pr`) to avoid confusion. The remote default is `origin/Staging` (`origin/HEAD -> origin/Staging`); there is no separate lowercase branch.

When branching for a fix, verify state explicitly: `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` and `git rev-list --left-right --count Staging...origin/Staging` (local `Staging` may be ahead of `origin/Staging` by unpushed commits — branching off local `Staging` carries those into your PR).
